# Code owners for academicOps.
#
# GitHub automatically REQUESTS a review from the matching code owner(s) the
# moment a PR is opened (and again when new owned paths are touched), so the
# maintainer no longer has to discover PRs by browsing — they land in the
# owner's "Review requested" queue. This is the native affordance the PR
# pipeline relies on to surface PRs to the human admission gate
# (specs/workflows/pr-pipeline.md §3.2: a maintainer's review APPROVAL is the
# admission signal).
#
# Note: GitHub never requests review from the PR author, so PRs the maintainer
# opens themselves are not self-requested — only agent/bot-authored PRs
# (e.g. opened as `botnicbot`) generate the request, which is exactly the case
# that needs surfacing.
#
# This file drives auto-REQUEST only; it is intentionally NOT wired as a
# "require review from Code Owners" branch-protection rule — admission
# (`admit-status`), not a GitHub review count, is the merge gate
# (`required_approving_review_count: 0`, ruleset 13762049). Adding owner-review
# enforcement would be a deliberate, separate spec change.

